   "html_text": "After these attempts at modernizing the epic, the next phase of the Quarrel of the Ancients and the Moderns focused on other aspects of modern life. This time, Boileau faced a new opponent, Charles Perrault, now best known as a compiler of fairy tales. In fact, fairy tales were significant because they celebrated the European oral tradition that did not have Greco-Roman roots, in contrast to the fables of La Fontaine, who was a partisan of the Ancients. Perrault took a stand for the Modern side ",
   "md_text": "After these attempts at modernizing the epic, the next phase of the Quarrel of the Ancients and the Moderns focused on other aspects of modern life. This time, Boileau faced a new opponent, Charles Perrault, now best known as a compiler of fairy tales. In fact, fairy tales were significant because they celebrated the European oral tradition that did not have Greco-Roman roots, in contrast to the fables of La Fontaine, who was a partisan of the Ancients. Perrault took a stand for the Modern side "
